| Fail on drift | {{FACTORY-BOOL:observability.driftDetection.failOnDrift}} |
| Open issue | {{FACTORY-BOOL:observability.driftDetection.openIssueOnDrift}} |
#{{ELSE}}
Not configured — set `observability.driftDetection` in `lz-config.json` to
enable scheduled drift detection.
#{{ENDIF}}

Drift jobs are read-only. A finding opens a tracked remediation path; it must
never silently apply or import resources.

## SLO guidance

Measure workflow availability, apply success rate, mean time to detect drift,
mean time to restore state, policy-compliance percentage, diagnostic coverage,
backup success, and alert delivery. Set workload-specific objectives outside
this platform baseline.

## Validation

After bootstrap and each material change:

1. generate a test platform-health alert;
2. verify Activity Log ingestion and retention;
3. verify Entra sign-in diagnostics;
4. confirm each active layer appears in workflow telemetry;
5. run drift detection against a clean deployment;
6. validate alert ownership and escalation.

